== History==
2017
*The Bats were once available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Bats Draft Challenge]], which started on 23/6/2017. In this challenge, gameplay was similar to a regular Draft Challenge, except that one of the players was able to choose who would use the Bats. If the player achieved at least 8 wins, they obtained the Bats early.
*From 30/6/2017 through 3/7/2017, the [[Shop]] had a special offer where [[Arenas|Arena]] 8+ players could buy up to 6 Giant [[Chests]] at the normal price that guarantee at least 40% of the Chest's contents to be Bats.
*The Bats [[Cards|card]] was generally released on 7/7/2017.
*On 11/8/2017, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (11/8/2017)|Balance Update]], increased the unit count to 5 (from 4).
*On 9/10/2017, the [[Version History#Epic Quests Update (9/10/2017)|Epic Quests Update]], changed the card description. Prior to this update, it read "''Five tiny flying creatures with big ears. Having big ears doesn't mean they'll listen when asked to stop attacking you''".
2018 
*On 12/1/2018, the Bats were added to the [[Touchdown]] Draft,
*On 24/1/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (24/1/2018)|Balance Update]], increased the Bats' attack time interval to 1.1 seconds (from 1 second) and increased their first attack time interval to 0.6 seconds (from 0.5 seconds).
*On 25/4/2018, the [[Version History#Clan%20Wars%20Update%20(25/4/2018)|Clan Wars Update]], changed the description. It used to read "''Spawns a handful of tiny flying creatures with big ears. Having big ears doesn't mean they're good listeners.''"
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Bats from Frozen Peak to Spell Valley.
2019
*On 4/3/2019, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/3/2019)|Balance Update]], gave the Bats a new 0.15 seconds deploy stagger from each other.
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], added a card render to the Bats' card info screen.
2020
*On 2/6/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (2/6/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the deploy stagger for each Bat to 0.1 seconds (from 0.15 seconds).
*On 4/8/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/8/2020)|Balance Update]], increased the Bats' attack time interval to 1.3 seconds (from 1.1 seconds) and increased their first attack time interval to 0.8 seconds (from 0.6 seconds).
*On 9/12/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (9/12/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the Bats' first attack time interval to 0.6 seconds (from 0.8 seconds).
2021
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Bats from Spell Valley to Builder's Workshop.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
*On 2/10/2023, the [https://clashroyale.fandom.com/wiki/Version_History#Pass_Royale_and_more_(2/10/2023) October 2023 Update], added the Bats' Evolution.
2025
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], made it so that Bats' spawn formation would be correctly mirrored depending on which side of the Arena they were placed.
2026

* On 2/3/2026, a Balance Update, decreased the Bats' hitpoints to 1.2 seconds (from 1.3 seconds).

